---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/sendlane-vs-klaviyo';
const title = 'Sendlane vs Klaviyo for Shopify Email: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Sendlane vs Klaviyo for Shopify: audit existing events, flow dependencies, migration scope and billing before replacing a retention platform.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Should a higher Klaviyo bill trigger migration?",
    "answer": "It should trigger a billing and audience review. Compare current quotes and the cost of repairing the existing setup before committing to rebuilding it."
  },
  {
    "question": "How can I compare Shopify browse tracking?",
    "answer": "Check app-embed and integration settings, then map an actual collection-view to purchase sequence. Compare event properties, identity and flow exits in each candidate."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is guided migration automatically included with Sendlane?",
    "answer": "Do not assume a universal scope. Obtain a written proposal covering records, forms, flows, approvals and support after cutover."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Sendlane vs Klaviyo</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sendlane vs Klaviyo for Shopify email</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">A Shopify team considering Sendlane as an alternative to Klaviyo should first separate a configuration problem from an unmet requirement. Sendlane markets unified email, SMS and forms; Klaviyo documents Shopify event tracking and store integration. Neither a rising bill nor a neglected flow proves that migration will fix the underlying work.</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Start with the reason for leaving</h2>
        <p>Write the actual problem in observable terms: a collection-view event is missing, a recent purchaser receives a promotion, a campaign takes too many approval handoffs, or the bill no longer matches the planned audience. Avoid translating every problem into “Klaviyo complexity.” Missing ownership and incorrect setup can persist after a platform change.</p>
        <p>For each problem, identify the current configuration, desired behavior and cost of repairing it in place. Ask Sendlane to demonstrate the replacement behavior with the same inputs. This creates a repair-versus-migrate decision instead of a broad claim that one platform has better data or more helpful people.</p>
        <h2>Audit tracking before comparing browse workflows</h2>
        <p>Klaviyo’s Shopify setup guide distinguishes app-embed tracking from integration settings. It describes Viewed Product and Active on Site tracking and optional behavioral events including Viewed Collection, Submitted Search and Added to Cart. A missing event can therefore be a setup issue; seeing an integration marked connected is not sufficient.</p>
        <p>Proposed exercise, not an executed test: a home-goods store visits a lamp collection, views one variant, adds it to cart and then purchases. Capture the event names and properties available to each candidate. Ask Sendlane to show how the same sequence enters and exits its automation. Compare identity, product identifiers and timing rather than assuming every similarly named event has identical meaning.</p>
        <h2>Translate dependencies before moving a flow</h2>
        <p>Inventory every condition in the existing Klaviyo flows: event properties, profile fields, lists, segments, catalog references and any external subscription data. Mark which are essential and which accumulated without a clear purpose. A screenshot of the flow canvas does not preserve the definitions of its inputs.</p>
        <p>For a high-consideration lamp purchase, separate product education from a discount reminder. Specify how a new order, refund or change of product interest affects eligibility. Ask the replacement vendor to map each essential condition. If a field or behavior cannot be reproduced, record the business consequence before deciding whether a simpler workflow is acceptable.</p>
        <h2>Make migration assistance contractual</h2>
        <p>Sendlane’s current public positioning establishes an ecommerce platform, not a universal promise to recreate every custom flow or provide quarterly reviews. Ask for the offered migration scope in writing: historical records, templates, forms, automations, authentication and support after cutover. Apply the same scrutiny to a Klaviyo partner or internal repair project.</p>
        <p>Name the person who accepts each migrated flow and the evidence they need: correct audience, valid links, matching product content and a tested purchase exit. An external team may provide capacity, but the store still needs someone to approve business rules. Do not assume a package replaces ongoing ownership.</p>
        <h2>Compare bills against the same sending plan</h2>
        <p>Use a current quote for the intended audience and volume. Include email limits, profile or contact treatment, SMS destinations and credits, onboarding, retained integrations and any paid assistance. Ask how suppression, dormant records and a seasonal campaign change each bill. This article does not establish a price premium for either vendor.</p>
        <p>A larger bill can justify a review without justifying migration. Estimate the work of rebuilding forms, product blocks and dependencies alongside recurring charges. Keep projected savings separate from measured savings, and do not count attributed flow revenue as incremental profit from the proposed switch.</p>
        <h2>Choose a cutover with an acceptance boundary</h2>
        <p>Before enabling replacement messages, assign each flow to one sender and define rollback conditions. Preserve unsubscribe and channel-permission records. Validate audience differences and prevent overlapping cart recovery. Remove obsolete forms and tracking only after their remaining jobs are accounted for. There is no universal safe number of parallel weeks.</p>
        <p>Stay with a repaired Klaviyo configuration when it meets the requirement and migration adds no useful capability. Consider Sendlane when the demonstrated workflow and written implementation scope resolve a concrete problem the team cannot reasonably solve in place. No browse-depth ranking, revenue guarantee or fixed merchant-size threshold follows from this comparison.</p>
        <h2>Primary sources and limits</h2>
        <p>Reviewed November 25, 2026. These sources establish advertised scope, not results from our own product tests. Account configuration, quotes and the proposed exercises remain unverified.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005080407">Klaviyo Shopify setup guide</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://www.sendlane.com/">Sendlane product positioning</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/sendlane-app">Sendlane Shopify listing</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/drip-vs-sendlane">Drip vs Sendlane</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-omnisend">Klaviyo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/home-goods">Email apps for home goods stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Sendlane vs Klaviyo FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
